# Basic boiler Plate Doc | Grade A
# Why this file exists: Keeps build artefacts, virtualenvs and local state out of the repository.
# Grade A here: nothing in this file is specific to this project. Copy it unchanged.
# Grades: A copy into a new project as is, no edits. B copy it and swap the
# names, paths or patterns named above. C leave behind, it is this project's
# own content rather than scaffolding, and is not tagged.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Node
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Terraform
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
# A stray tfvars anywhere is ignored, because that is where somebody puts a
# secret while debugging.
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
# The environment files under envs/ are the exception and are committed. They
# hold sizes, counts and retention windows, no secrets, and `make tf-plan`
# names them directly: ignoring them would leave the deploy targets pointing at
# files that cannot exist after a clone. Every secret they would otherwise
# carry, the ExternalId, the certificate and the alert topics, is passed at
# apply time instead, and production refuses to start without the last three.
!infra/terraform/*/envs/*.tfvars
.terraform.tfstate.lock.info
# .terraform.lock.hcl is deliberately NOT ignored. It pins the exact provider
# versions and their checksums, which is the same reproducibility argument that
# pins base images by digest in docker/base-images.lock. Ignoring it lets `~> 6.0`
# resolve to a different provider in the pipeline than on a contributor's machine,
# and the difference shows up as a plan nobody can reproduce.

# Secrets and local config
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
*.pem
*.key
local-auth.yaml
!local-auth.example.yaml

# Editors and OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Scratch
scratch/
tmp/

# Claude Code local session state
.claude/state/
# Local tool state under the web app, and personal documents: never part of the product. Both
# were committed by mistake once and removed from the history on 2026-10-13, before the first
# push to a remote.
finops-web/.claude/
finops-web/src/.claude/
*.docx

# The generated API reference. Published as a pipeline artifact rather than
# stored, because it is 4 MB of derived HTML that changes on every docstring.
docs/api/

# The exported fake utilization estate. Deterministic build output from
# `finops_providers/fake/`, so the generators are the source and the CSV is not:
# 29 MB of derived rows, regenerable with one command. It would also be refused
# on the way in, because a twelve digit byte count reads as a hardcoded value to
# `scripts/security/check_hardcoded.py`.
files.zip
meter-fake-estate-data-*.zip
fake-estate/
